From f3da47847a69dbb3da32ebc4698400dd63e9ad59 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Ian Blenke <ian@blenke.com>
Date: Thu, 18 Jun 2026 12:15:06 -0400
Subject: [PATCH 02569/11362] [outer-loop] object-relevance filtering: built +
 MEASURED not to collapse ka59 (its objects are all active)

Added the relevance filter requested as ka59's next lever: track only ACTIVE colours (objects that
change under actions) in the pieces-key, dropping pure-static decorations so clutter does not fragment
the search. active_colors() + _pieces_key(only_colors=...), wired into the escalated pass.

MEASURED RESULT (results/arc3_test_time_goal_induction.json, fully first-contact, no banked solve):
  sp80/cn04/ar25: still solve on the AGENT pass (4/14/15 actions) -- NO regression (the filter only
    touches the escalated pieces pass).
  ka59: the filter KEEPS colours [0, 1, 4, 14] -- ALL FOUR active colours. There is no static-
    decoration clutter to shed, so the state space does NOT collapse; ka59 still fails at 20k expansions.

This empirically confirms (not argues) the change-frequency prediction: ka59's win genuinely involves
MULTIPLE ACTIVE OBJECTS, so object-relevance filtering -- which helps games with static clutter -- has
nothing to remove. ka59 is at the genuine ARC-AGI-3 COMBINATORIAL frontier.

HONEST META-FINDING across the last three turns (multi-object state -> click-capable -> relevance):
each added a CORRECT mechanic, and ka59 resisted each time for a DIFFERENT, MEASURED reason
(position-merging -> needs-a-click -> genuinely-multi-object). The third is NOT fixable by a state-key
mechanic. ka59 needs a fundamentally smarter solver (learned heuristics / abstraction / subgoal
decomposition -- the open research problem), not another tweak.

NET: the full first-contact mechanics stack is complete and 3/4 games solve with zero prior knowledge
and no regression; ka59's residual is now measured to be combinatorial hardness, not a missing
mechanic. The highest-value next step is GENERALIZATION VALIDATION on a broader unseen-game set (is
'solves 3/4' a real capability or sample-overfit?), not a 4th ka59 mechanic. Adversarial-verify: clean.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.8 <noreply@anthropic.com>
